---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import {
  COMPANY_NAME,
  COMPANY_LOCATION,
  COMPANY_STRUCTURE,
  FOUNDER_NAME,
  RESEARCH_BEGAN_YEAR,
  LEGAL_FORMATION_YEAR,
} from '../data/company';
---

<Layout
  title="About ByteLite LLC"
  description="ByteLite LLC is a founder-led research company in Helena, Montana developing ByteLite, a deterministic lossless data-representation architecture."
  keywords="ByteLite LLC, Helena Montana, founder-led research"
  canonical="https://www.thebytelite.com/about/"
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>{COMPANY_NAME}</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        Founder-led technology research and development focused on ByteLite, in {COMPANY_LOCATION}. The research
        work began in {RESEARCH_BEGAN_YEAR}; {COMPANY_NAME} was formed in {LEGAL_FORMATION_YEAR}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>The work.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Data is expensive to keep and to move. ByteLite is being developed as a deterministic
        lossless representation architecture, with the target of producing a smaller
        self-contained representation for every source file, from which the exact
        original can be reconstructed. That target is still being engineered and proven.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt">The proof philosophy.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Exact reconstruction comes first, because a system that cannot return the original has not
        earned the right to talk about size. Any size claim is counted from the complete artifact
        &mdash; not estimated, and not with part of the cost moved somewhere uncounted.
      </p>
      <p class="body">
        Where something has not been proven, this site says so. I am still building this, and
        saying so plainly is better than polished language that makes unfinished work sound
        finished.
      </p>

      {/* The <ol> below, not the image, carries the meaning: the image's sub-labels render at
          roughly 5px at a 320px viewport, so they cannot be the only copy. Nothing here marks a
          position on the ladder - ByteLite's current rung is stated once, on /validation, and a
          second copy could drift out of step with the evidence. Full rationale in
          ASSET_MANIFEST.md, "Website Graphics Refresh Pass". */}
      <figure class="ladder-fig">
        <img src="/bytelite/proof-before-claim-ladder.webp"
             alt="Proof-before-claim progression from concept through prototype, proof artifact, validation, and product."
             width="1400" height="788" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>Claims rise only when the evidence behind them rises.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <ol class="ladder">
        <li><span class="ladder-rung">Concept</span><span class="ladder-note">Idea defined.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ladder-rung">Prototype</span><span class="ladder-note">System explored.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ladder-rung">Proof artifact</span><span class="ladder-note">Reproducible output.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ladder-rung">Validation</span><span class="ladder-note">Tested against criteria.</span></li>
        <li><span class="ladder-rung">Product</span><span class="ladder-note">Public-facing delivery.</span></li>
      </ol>

      <p class="body">
        This ladder is the standard applied to every statement on this site. It is not a progress
        report: which rung ByteLite currently occupies is recorded in one place only, with the
        evidence behind it, on the <a href="/validation">validation page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt">Commercial intent.</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Personal use is planned as a flat subscription, priced so that one large file can never
        become an unexpected bill. Business and enterprise licensing is planned against a 50/50
        share of verified qualifying savings, so the company earns only when a measured saving
        exists. Both depend on validation that is still in progress.
      </p>

      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Company</dt><dd>{COMPANY_NAME}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>{COMPANY_LOCATION}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Structure</dt><dd>{COMPANY_STRUCTURE}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Founder</dt><dd>{FOUNDER_NAME}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Research began</dt><dd>{RESEARCH_BEGAN_YEAR}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>LLC formed</dt><dd>{LEGAL_FORMATION_YEAR}</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/validation" class="btn btn-outline">Current evidence</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
.narrow { max-width: 780px; }
.page-hero { padding: 4rem 0 2rem; }
.hero-sub { max-width: 640px; font-size: 1.0625rem; margin-top: 1rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; }
h2 { margin-bottom: .75rem; }
.mt { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
.body { font-size: 1rem; color: #a0a8c0; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: 1rem; }
/* Constrained by .narrow (780px), never upscaled past its intrinsic 1400px. width/height sit on
   the tag so the 16:9 box is reserved before the bytes land - no shift on a slow connection. */
.ladder-fig { margin: 2rem 0 0; }
.ladder-fig img {
  display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;
  border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .75rem; background: #0d1120;
}
.ladder-fig figcaption { margin-top: .75rem; font-size: .875rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.6; }
.ladder {
  list-style: none; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; counter-reset: rung;
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .75rem;
}
@media (max-width: 700px) { .ladder { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.ladder li {
  counter-increment: rung; padding: .875rem 1rem;
  background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-left: 3px solid #6366f1;
  border-radius: .5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .25rem;
}
.ladder li::before { content: counter(rung); font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 700; color: #555e7a; }
.ladder-rung { font-size: .9375rem; font-weight: 500; color: #e4e7f2; }
.ladder-note { font-size: .8125rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.5; }

.facts {
  margin: 2.5rem 0 0; padding: 1.5rem;
  background: #0d1120; border: 1px solid #1a2235; border-radius: .75rem;
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem 2rem;
}
@media (max-width: 560px) { .facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.facts dt { font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #555e7a; }
.facts dd { margin: .2rem 0 0; font-size: .9375rem; color: #e4e7f2; }
.cta-row { display: flex; gap: .75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
